; definite shape and definite volume. the atoms/molecules are fixed in place.
; thermal motion is vibration around equilibrium positions — not translation.
; the binding energy between particles exceeds thermal energy: kT < bond energy.
; 
; two types:
; crystalline: atoms in ordered periodic lattice. definite melting point.
; most metals, ionic compounds, many minerals.
; unit cell repeats in 3D — the symmetry determines all properties.
; amorphous:   no long-range order. glass transition temperature, not melting point.
; glass, most plastics, rubber, gels.
; 
; mechanical properties of solids:
; elastic deformation:  stress removed → returns to shape (Hooke's law)
; plastic deformation:  stress exceeds yield point → permanent deformation
; fracture:             stress exceeds fracture point → breaks
; hardness:             resistance to indentation (Mohs scale, Vickers)
; 
; in 3d / pratibimba: solid objects have fixed mesh geometry.
; the mesh does not flow or deform under gravity in real time.
; collision: coefficient-of-restitution applies. normal-force applies.
; physics connections
; 3d / pratibimba

